IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IV: sections 85 and 86 (assessment of an employer and recovery of
-- what it owes: the debt, the deemed trust, the certificate a responsible representative needs, security).
-- Written by piece ei3 (Sonnet 5.5). LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Unofficial plain-text source; nothing verified
-- against the official text.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as inputs: the Income Tax Act's "security interest" and "secured creditor" (s 224(1.3), not deposited);
-- the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act (not deposited); the outcome of an appeal under ss 91, 92 or 103 (this piece, other modules).

§ `Section 85 - assessment`

-- Subsection (1): the Minister (of National Revenue in Part IV) may assess for "an amount payable by the employer under this
-- Act", and may reassess or make additional assessments; "assessment" in the Act includes both.
-- src:1362 | 85 (1) The Minister may assess an employer for an amount payable by the employer under this Act, or may reassess the employer or make such additional assessments as the circumstances require, and the expression “assessment” when used in this Act with reference to any action so taken by the Minister under this section includes a reassessment or an additional assessment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(1) (src:1362)
GIVEN `the amount is payable by the employer under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(1) the Minister may assess the employer` IF
    `the amount is payable by the employer under this Act`

-- src:1362 | 85 (1) The Minister may assess an employer for an amount payable by the employer under this Act, or may reassess the employer or make such additional assessments as the circumstances require, and the expression “assessment” when used in this Act with reference to any action so taken by the Minister under this section includes a reassessment or an additional assessment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(1) (src:1362)
GIVEN `the action is an assessment, a reassessment or an additional assessment made by the Minister under section 85` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(1) the action is an assessment` IF
    `the action is an assessment, a reassessment or an additional assessment made by the Minister under section 85`

-- Subsection (2): once the notice of assessment is sent the assessment is valid and binding, subject to being vacated or varied
-- on appeal, and the employer is liable to pay the amount to Her Majesty without delay.
-- src:1364 | (2) After assessing an employer for an amount payable under this Act, the Minister shall send the employer a notice of assessment, and when the notice is sent the assessment is valid and binding subject to being vacated or varied on appeal under this Act, and the employer is liable to pay the amount to Her Majesty without delay.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(2) (src:1364)
GIVEN `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(2) the assessment is valid and binding` IF
        `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment`
    AND (NOT `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act`)

-- src:1364 | (2) After assessing an employer for an amount payable under this Act, the Minister shall send the employer a notice of assessment, and when the notice is sent the assessment is valid and binding subject to being vacated or varied on appeal under this Act, and the employer is liable to pay the amount to Her Majesty without delay.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(2) (src:1364)
GIVEN `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(2) the employer is liable to pay the amount to Her Majesty without delay` IF
    `s 85(2) the assessment is valid and binding` `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act`

-- Subsection (3): no assessment "after three years have elapsed after the end of the year in which any premium in relation
-- to which that amount is payable should have been paid", unless misrepresentation or fraud in filing a return or supplying
-- information about it. Three years after the end of year Y is the end of 31 December Y+3: an assessment made on that day is
-- not "after" (fork F-ei3-14).
-- src:1366 | (3) No assessment, reassessment or additional assessment of an amount payable by an employer under this Act may be made by the Minister under this section after three years have elapsed after the end of the year in which any premium in relation to which that amount is payable should have been paid, unless the employer has made a misrepresentation or committed fraud in filing a return or in supplying information about the return under this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(3) (src:1366)
GIVEN `the year in which the premium should have been paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the Minister makes the assessment` IS A DATE
      `the employer has made a misrepresentation or committed fraud in filing a return or in supplying information about the return under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 85(3) the Minister may make the assessment on that day` IF
        `the employer has made a misrepresentation or committed fraud in filing a return or in supplying information about the return under this Part`
    OR  `the day on which the Minister makes the assessment` AT MOST (`add years` (YearMonthDay `the year in which the premium should have been paid` 12 31) 3)

-- Subsection (4): the day of mailing or sending is deemed to be the date appearing on the notice, "in the absence of any evidence
-- to the contrary" and unless the Minister (or a person acting for the Minister or Her Majesty) calls it into question.
-- Otherwise the deeming does not apply (NOTHING): the day is then a matter of evidence.
-- src:1368 | (4) The day of mailing or sending, as the case may be, of a notice of assessment described in subsection (2) is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, deemed to be the day appearing from the notice to be the date of the notice unless called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(4) (src:1368)
GIVEN `the date appearing from the notice to be the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date is called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 85(4) the day of mailing or sending the notice of assessment is deemed to be` IS
    IF (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) AND (NOT `the date is called into question by the Minister or by a person acting for the Minister or for Her Majesty`)
    THEN JUST `the date appearing from the notice to be the date of the notice`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (5): an electronic notice is presumed sent and received on the date an electronic message is sent, to the address
-- most recently provided before that date, saying that a notice needing immediate attention is in the person's secure
-- electronic account. A notice is "made available" if posted there, the person has authorized that and has not revoked it.
-- Otherwise there is no presumption (NOTHING).
-- src:1370 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, if a notice or other communication in respect of a person or partnership is made available in electronic format such that it can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system or other similar device, the notice or other communication is presumed to be sent to the person or partnership and received by the person or partnership on the date that an electronic message is sent, to the electronic address most recently provided before that date by the person or partnership to the Minister for the purposes of this subsection, informing the person or partnership that a notice or other communication requiring the person or partnership’s immediate attention is available in the person or partnership’s secure electronic account. A notice or other communication is considered to be made available if it is posted by the Minister in the person or partnership’s secure electronic account and the person or partnership has authorized that notices or other communications may be made available in this manner and has not before that date revoked that authorization in a manner specified by the Minister.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 85(5) (src:1370)
GIVEN `the notice or communication is made available in electronic format such that it can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was posted by the Minister in the secure electronic account of the person or partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or partnership has authorized notices to be made available in this manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or partnership has revoked that authorization before that date in a manner specified by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an electronic message was sent to the electronic address most recently provided before that date by the person or partnership to the Minister for the purposes of subsection 85(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message informed them that a notice or other communication requiring their immediate attention is available in their secure electronic account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the electronic message was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 85(5) the day on which the notice is presumed to be sent and received` IS
    IF     `the notice or communication is made available in electronic format such that it can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system`
       AND `it was posted by the Minister in the secure electronic account of the person or partnership`
       AND `the person or partnership has authorized notices to be made available in this manner`
       AND (NOT `the person or partnership has revoked that authorization before that date in a manner specified by the Minister`)
       AND `an electronic message was sent to the electronic address most recently provided before that date by the person or partnership to the Minister for the purposes of subsection 85(5)`
       AND `the message informed them that a notice or other communication requiring their immediate attention is available in their secure electronic account`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the electronic message was sent`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 86 - recovery`

-- src:1372 | 86 (1) All premiums, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by an employer under this Act are debts due to Her Majesty and are recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided for by this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(1) (src:1372)
GIVEN `the amount is a premium, interest, penalty or other amount payable by an employer under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(1) the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` IF
    `the amount is a premium, interest, penalty or other amount payable by an employer under this Act`

-- Subsection (2): an amount deducted as an employee's premium and not remitted is deemed held in trust for Her Majesty,
-- separate from the employer's property and from property held by a secured creditor, notwithstanding any security interest.
-- src:1374 | (2) Where an employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as or on account of any employee’s premium required to be paid by the insured person but has not remitted the amount to the Receiver General, the employer is deemed, notwithstanding any security interest (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) in the amount so deducted, to hold the amount separate and apart from the property of the employer and from property held by any secured creditor (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) of that employer that but for the security interest would be property of the employer, in trust for Her Majesty and for payment to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2) (src:1374)
GIVEN `the employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as or on account of an employee's premium required to be paid by the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has not remitted the amount to the Receiver General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(2) the employer is deemed to hold the amount in trust for Her Majesty` IF
        `the employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an insured person as or on account of an employee's premium required to be paid by the insured person`
    AND `the employer has not remitted the amount to the Receiver General`

-- Subsection (2.1): at any time an amount is deemed held in trust under (2), property of the employer and of a secured creditor,
-- equal in value, (a) is deemed held in trust for Her Majesty from the time the amount was deducted and (b) is deemed to form no
-- part of the employer's estate from that time; it is beneficially owned by Her Majesty and its proceeds go to the Receiver
-- General in priority to the security interests. The four rules below are the four limbs of that one sentence.
-- src:1376 | (2.1) Notwithstanding the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act (except sections 81.1 and 81.2 of that Act), any other enactment of Canada, any enactment of a province or any other law, where at any time an amount deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act, property of the employer and property held by any secured creditor (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) of that employer that but for a security interest (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) would be property of the employer, equal in value to the amount so deemed to be held in trust is deemed
-- src:1377 | (a) to be held, from the time the amount was deducted by the employer, separate and apart from the property of the employer, in trust for Her Majesty whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest, and
-- src:1378 | (b) to form no part of the estate or property of the employer from the time the amount was so deducted, whether or not the property has in fact been kept separate and apart from the estate or property of the employer and whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest
-- src:1379 | and is property beneficially owned by Her Majesty notwithstanding any security interest in such property or in the proceeds thereof, and the proceeds of such property shall be paid to the Receiver General in priority to all such security interests.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2.1) (src:1376-1379)
GIVEN `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(2.1) property equal in value to the amount is deemed to be held in trust for Her Majesty` IF
    `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty`

-- src:1377 | (a) to be held, from the time the amount was deducted by the employer, separate and apart from the property of the employer, in trust for Her Majesty whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2.1)(a) (src:1377)
GIVEN `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the amount was deducted by the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 86(2.1)(a) the day from which the property is deemed to be held in trust` IS
    IF `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the amount was deducted by the employer`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1378 | (b) to form no part of the estate or property of the employer from the time the amount was so deducted, whether or not the property has in fact been kept separate and apart from the estate or property of the employer and whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2.1)(b) (src:1378)
GIVEN `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(2.1)(b) the property is deemed to form no part of the estate or property of the employer` IF
    `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty`

-- src:1379 | and is property beneficially owned by Her Majesty notwithstanding any security interest in such property or in the proceeds thereof, and the proceeds of such property shall be paid to the Receiver General in priority to all such security interests.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2.1) (src:1379)
GIVEN `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(2.1) the proceeds of the property shall be paid to the Receiver General in priority to all security interests` IF
    `an amount is deemed by subsection (2) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty`

-- src:1381 | (2.2) For the purposes of subsections (2) and (2.1), a security interest does not include a prescribed security interest.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(2.2) (src:1381)
GIVEN `is a security interest as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a prescribed security interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(2.2) the interest is a security interest for the purposes of subsections (2) and (2.1)` IF
        `is a security interest as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act`
    AND (NOT `is a prescribed security interest`)

-- Subsection (3): before distributing property over which it has control in that capacity, the responsible representative must
-- obtain a certificate certifying payment, or the Minister's acceptance of security for payment, of two classes of amount.
-- src:1383 | (3) Before distributing any property over which a responsible representative has control in that capacity, the responsible representative shall obtain a certificate from the Minister certifying the payment, or acceptance by the Minister of security for payment, of all amounts
-- src:1384 | (a) for which an employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution; and
-- src:1385 | (b) for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable in that capacity.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(3) (src:1383-1385)
GIVEN `has control of the property in the capacity of responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is about to distribute it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(3) the responsible representative shall obtain a certificate from the Minister before distributing` IF
        `has control of the property in the capacity of responsible representative`
    AND `is about to distribute it`

-- src:1383 | (3) Before distributing any property over which a responsible representative has control in that capacity, the responsible representative shall obtain a certificate from the Minister certifying the payment, or acceptance by the Minister of security for payment, of all amounts
-- src:1384 | (a) for which an employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution; and
-- src:1385 | (b) for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable in that capacity.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(3) (src:1383-1385)
GIVEN `the certificate certifies the payment, or acceptance of security for payment, of all amounts for which an employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate certifies the payment, or acceptance of security for payment, of all amounts for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(3) the certificate is the certificate the subsection requires` IF
        `the certificate certifies the payment, or acceptance of security for payment, of all amounts for which an employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution`
    AND `the certificate certifies the payment, or acceptance of security for payment, of all amounts for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable in that capacity`

-- Subsection (4): distributing without the certificate makes the responsible representative personally liable "to the extent of
-- the value of the property distributed"; the Minister may assess them as under section 85.
-- src:1387 | (4) If the responsible representative distributes to one or more persons property over which the responsible representative has control in that capacity, without obtaining the certificate, the responsible representative is personally liable for the payment of the amounts to the extent of the value of the property distributed and the Minister may assess the responsible representative for the amounts in the same manner and with the same effect as an assessment made under section 85.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(4) (src:1387)
GIVEN `distributes to one or more persons property over which the responsible representative has control in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `did so without obtaining the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(4) the responsible representative is personally liable` IF
        `distributes to one or more persons property over which the responsible representative has control in that capacity`
    AND `did so without obtaining the certificate`

-- src:1387 | (4) If the responsible representative distributes to one or more persons property over which the responsible representative has control in that capacity, without obtaining the certificate, the responsible representative is personally liable for the payment of the amounts to the extent of the value of the property distributed and the Minister may assess the responsible representative for the amounts in the same manner and with the same effect as an assessment made under section 85.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(4) (src:1387)
GIVEN `the amounts described in paragraphs 86(3)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property distributed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 86(4) the extent of the personal liability` IS
    IF `the value of the property distributed` LESS THAN `the amounts described in paragraphs 86(3)(a) and (b)`
    THEN `the value of the property distributed`
    ELSE `the amounts described in paragraphs 86(3)(a) and (b)`

-- src:1389 | (5) If the Minister considers it advisable in a particular case, the Minister may accept security for payment of premiums by way of mortgage, hypothec or other charge of any kind whatever on property of the employer or any other person or by way of guarantee from other persons.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(5) (src:1389)
GIVEN `the Minister considers it advisable in a particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is a mortgage, hypothec or other charge of any kind on property of the employer or any other person, or a guarantee from other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(5) the Minister may accept the security for payment of premiums` IF
        `the Minister considers it advisable in a particular case`
    AND `the security is a mortgage, hypothec or other charge of any kind on property of the employer or any other person, or a guarantee from other persons`

-- src:1391 | (6) If an employer has become bankrupt, the trustee in bankruptcy is deemed to be the agent of the bankrupt for the purposes of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(6) (src:1391)
GIVEN `the employer has become bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the trustee in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(6) the trustee in bankruptcy is deemed to be the agent of the bankrupt for the purposes of this Act` IF
        `the employer has become bankrupt`
    AND `the person is the trustee in bankruptcy`

-- Subsection (7): a person "other than a trustee in bankruptcy" who is an assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager,
-- administrator, executor, liquidator of the succession "or any other like person administering, winding up, controlling or
-- otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person". The administering words are read as qualifying
-- the whole list (fork F-ei3-15).
-- src:1393 | (7) For the purposes of this section, responsible representative means a person, other than a trustee in bankruptcy, who is an assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager, administrator, executor, liquidator of the succession or any other like person administering, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 86(7) (src:1393)
GIVEN `is a trustee in bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager, administrator, executor, liquidator of the succession or any other like person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is administering, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 86(7) responsible representative` IF
        (NOT `is a trustee in bankruptcy`)
    AND `is an assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager, administrator, executor, liquidator of the succession or any other like person`
    AND `is administering, winding up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person`
